WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.000
Pick up the clamp with the nearest arm,
transfer it to the other arm, then place it in the blue bin.

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:05.167
The right arm grasps near the base of a handle
and lifts the clamp from the table.

00:00:05.167 --> 00:00:09.334
Early proposals were rejected for IK or collision.
Gemini revised the approach to a tilted receiving grasp.

00:00:09.333 --> 00:00:18.333
Turn 9: the left gripper closes on the exposed handle.
The right gripper continues holding the clamp.

00:00:18.333 --> 00:00:20.833
Turn 10: request a fresh observation and inspect the grip.
Release is kept separate from the next movement.

00:00:20.833 --> 00:00:26.833
Turn 11: open the right gripper in a separate plan.
The left gripper retains the clamp.

00:00:26.833 --> 00:00:29.500
Recheck holding, then move the giving arm away.
Receiver opening stays near 0.18 after release.

00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:32.500
The receiving arm carries the clamp to the bin
and aligns it for placement.

00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:35.667
Release the clamp inside the blue bin.
Both arms return home.

00:00:35.667 --> 00:00:39.667
18 model turns | 18 executed segments | no drops
502.7 s total: 267.9 s inference, 154.4 s review, 46.3 s motion.

